{"id": 16, "ts": 1781185202.375131, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability and stress resilience, but I think we need to weigh Candidate\u202fC\u2019s strengths more heavily before finalising a decision.\u202fC is documented as \u201c100\u202f% reliable,\u201d which directly addresses operational reliability\u2014a core safety criterion.\u202fAdditionally, C \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d giving us clear evidence of high decision quality, something we have not seen for B.\u202fWhile C does have communication challenges (difficulty expressing ideas and being seen as egocentric), the notes also say C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d suggesting that his teamwork impact may be less detrimental than B\u2019s \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative\u201d demeanor, which can erode crew cohesion.\u202fGiven that reliability and rapid, correct decision\u2011making are paramount for long\u2011distance flights, I would shift my provisional vote to Candidate\u202fC, pending any further insight on his stress handling."}
