{"id": 20, "ts": 1781185277.044889, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I agree with Sarah\u2019s move toward Candidate\u202fC. The documented 100\u202f% operational reliability and the fact that C \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d directly address the two most safety\u2011critical criteria for long\u2011distance flights\u2014reliability and decision quality. C also \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d and \u201cunderstands complicated technology,\u201d covering stress resilience and technical competence. While C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude are concerns, the notes also say he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d suggesting his teamwork impact may be manageable. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, despite being conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, shows serious crew\u2011cooperation red flags (nasty remarks, pretentious tone) and a weak numeric memory that could affect attention to detail. Candidates\u202fA and\u202fD lack clear evidence of reliability or consistent crew cooperation. Therefore, based on the evidence we have, Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit."}
