{"id": 32, "ts": 1781185423.2734652, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain aligned with Emily\u2019s provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB.\u202fB\u2019s documented conscientiousness and proven stress\u2011resilience directly satisfy the operational reliability and stress\u2011resilience criteria, while his strong technical abilities (weather assessment and computer skills) address the technical\u2011competence requirement.\u202fAlthough his pretentious tone and occasional nasty remarks are noted, these communication issues appear more remediable than the deeper interpersonal barriers raised for Candidate\u202fC.\nThe new input on Candidate\u202fD confirms solid decision\u2011making \u2013 he \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately\u201d and \u201csolves problems extremely well\u201d \u2013 and his sense of responsibility is a plus.\u202fHowever, the same notes flag a hot temper and a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude, and we still lack any evidence of crew\u2011cooperation.\u202fGiven that long\u2011haul flights demand consistent, constructive cockpit interaction, the temper risk outweighs D\u2019s decision\u2011making strength at this stage.\nCandidate\u202fA remains largely unevaluated on reliability, stress handling, and crew cooperation, so we cannot yet position him as a viable alternative.\nThus, based on the current evidence, I vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
